This repository is multi-licensed.

The majority of the code in this repository is licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt), unless stated otherwise.

Some files or directories are licensed differently, for example:
  - Small standalone utilities/examples may be MIT licensed
    (see LICENSES/MIT.txt)
  - Vendored or bundled third-party dependencies may carry their own
    license, e.g. GPL-3.0-or-later (see LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt)
  - Reference data, schema documentation, or datasets may be licensed under
    Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (see LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt)

The authoritative, per-file license is declared using an SPDX-License-Identifier
comment at the top of each file (or, where a header can't be added, via the
.reuse/dep5-style mapping in REUSE.toml). If there is any conflict between this
file and a file's own SPDX header, the per-file header governs that file.

This repository aims to comply with the REUSE specification (https://reuse.software)
so that licensing is machine-readable and auditable. Run `reuse lint` to verify.

Full license texts are provided, unmodified, in the LICENSES/ directory:
  - LICENSES/MIT.txt
  - LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt
  - LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt
  - LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt
